      {
        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": 8,
        "title": "When we talk plans, we normally work in English using the “going to” structure. Check the following examples.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "When we talk plans, we normally work in English using the “going to” structure. Check the following examples.",
          "TO CONSIDER 1. Going to is a fixed structure that denotes future. 2. The verbs after this grammatical structure go in simple form. 3. The future phrases at the end can be specific or general.",
          "Going to She is going to work as a community manager in the future. Is she going to work as a community manager in the future? They are going to become good traders at this rate. Are they going to become good traders at this rate? I am going to hitchhike so I can become a trip blogger. Are you going to hitchhike so you can become a trip blogger?"
        ],
        "links": [],
